Start from rest at origin so displacement is \vec{S} = \frac{1}{2} \vec{a} t^{2}
Acceleration \vec{a} = \vec{F} / m = (5 \hat{i} + 10 \hat{j}) / 0.1 = 50 \hat{i} + 100 \hat{j} m/s^{2}
In 2 s \vec{S} = \frac{1}{2}(50 \hat{i} + 100 \hat{j})(4) = 100 \hat{i} + 200 \hat{j} m
Given \vec{S} = 2x \hat{i} + 5y \hat{j} so 2x = 100 and 5y = 200 giving x = 50 and y = 40 → (D)

4035:
Figure shows disc hanging from horizontal tangent axis at rim point A
About a diameter in its plane centre moment is I_{cm} = \frac{1}{4} M R^{2}
Parallel axis to tangent rim gives I_A = \frac{1}{4} M R^{2} + M R^{2} = \frac{5}{4} M R^{2}
Pendulum period T = 2 \pi \sqrt{\frac{I_A}{M g R}} = 2 \pi \sqrt{\frac{5R}{4g}} → (A)

4036:
Torsional dipole frequency f = \frac{1}{2\pi}\sqrt{\frac{p E}{I}} is proportional to \sqrt{E}
Initial E_1 = E_0 with added 2E_0(\hat{j} + \hat{k}) perpendicular to E_0 \hat{i}
Net magnitude E = \sqrt{E_0^{2} + 4E_0^{2} + 4E_0^{2}} = 3E_0
Ratio f_2 / f_1 = \sqrt{3} \approx 1.732 so increase about 73 percent → (A)

4040:
Propagation is +x with \vec{B} along \hat{j} so \vec{E} \times \vec{B} must point along +\hat{i}
Since (-\hat{k}) \times \hat{j} = \hat{i} the field \vec{E} points along -\hat{k}
Magnitude E_0 = c B_0 with c = f \lambda where f is wave frequency
So \vec{E} = -f \lambda B_0 \sin(2\pi f t - 2\pi x / \lambda) \hat{k} → (A)

4044:
Accelerated wavelength \lambda = h / \sqrt{2 m q V} with same V
Electron and proton carry same charge magnitude so \lambda scales as 1/\sqrt{m}
Ratio gives \lambda_e / \lambda_p = \sqrt{m_p / m_e} → (A)

